# archive-intelligence — environment example
#
# The v0.1 engine requires NO environment variables: all configuration
# is file-based (see engine_config.example.json). This file documents
# the single optional variable the engine recognizes, for tooling that
# exports environment variables before running the modules.
#
# The engine does not read .env files itself. Export these in your
# shell, or let your process manager load them if you keep a .env file.

# Optional: path to an explicit engine configuration file.
# When unset, the engine discovers engine_config.json and
# engine_config.local.json at the workspace root.
# ENGINE_CONFIG=/absolute/path/to/engine_config.json
